('island-books', 'jersey', 'book', 'The Battle of the Strong', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Battle_of_the_Strong', 'The Battle of the Strong', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The book is set in the Channel Islands, primarily during the period 1781-95, and opens with attempted invasion of Jersey by France in the Battle of Jersey.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'wd-Q27508141', 'book', 'The Bondman', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bondman_%28novel%29', 'The Bondman (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The Bondman is an 1890 best-selling novel by Hall Caine set in the Isle of Man and Iceland.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-3469292', 'book', 'Catriona', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catriona_%28novel%29', 'Catriona (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'However, his attempts fail, as after being reunited with Alan Breck he is once again kidnapped, and held on the Bass Rock, an island prison in the Firth of Forth, until the trial is over, and James is condemned to death.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'wd-Q27508141', 'book', 'The Deemster', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Deemster', 'The Deemster', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'It was Caine''s third novel, the second to be set in the Isle of Man and it was his first great success.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'guernsey', 'book', 'The Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Guernsey_Literary_and_Potato_Peel_Pie_Society', 'The Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Isola Pribby, a member of the Society, believes that Dawsey is in love with Remy and, using Miss Marple as a model, offers to clean Dawsey''s home to find proof he is in love with Remy to convince her to stay in Guernsey.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-9603390', 'book', 'John of John', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_of_John', 'John of John', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The novel is set on the Isle of Harris in the Outer Hebrides of Scotland during the late 1990s.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-9620215', 'book', 'Kidnapped', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidnapped_%28novel%29', 'Kidnapped (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'David and Alan are separated in the confusion, with David being washed ashore on the isle of Erraid, near Mull, while Alan and the surviving crew row to safety on that same island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-3217444', 'book', 'Listen to the Moon', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Listen_to_the_Moon', 'Listen to the Moon', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Young Alfie Wheatcroft, his parents Jim and Mary and Uncle Billy live on the island of Bryher, and make a living by fishing and farming.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'wd-Q27508141', 'book', 'The Manxman', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Manxman_%28novel%29', 'The Manxman (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'A highly popular novel of its period, it was set in the Isle of Man and concerned a romantic triangle.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'rockall', 'book', 'The Master: An Adventure Story', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Master%3A_An_Adventure_Story', 'The Master: An Adventure Story', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'It involves two children, Judy and Nicky, and their dog Jokey, who are stranded on Rockall, an extremely small, uninhabited, remote rocky islet in the North Atlantic Ocean.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'mainland-orkney', 'book', 'The Outrun', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Outrun', 'The Outrun', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'It is set in Orkney, her childhood home, where she returned to rehabilitate after becoming an alcoholic in London.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'wd-Q27508141', 'book', 'Peveril of the Peak', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peveril_of_the_Peak', 'Peveril of the Peak', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Most of the story takes place in Derbyshire, London, and on the Isle of Man.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956937', 'book', 'Mr Pye', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mr_Pye', 'Mr Pye', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Mr. Pye travels to the Channel Island of Sark to awaken a love of God in all the islanders.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'wd-Q27508141', 'book', 'She''s All the World to Me', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/She%27s_All_the_World_to_Me', 'She''s All the World to Me', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The novel was the first of Caine''s works to be set on the Isle of Man and it centered on themes that would become integral to his later novels: a love triangle, secret mounting sins and eventual redemption.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'mainland-orkney', 'book', 'The Stronghold', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Stronghold_%28novel%29', 'The Stronghold (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Set in the Orkney islands during the 1st century BC, the story is an imaginative reconstruction of the development of the broch, the circular stronghold design of fortifications that dot the islands.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'isle-of-skye', 'book', 'To the Lighthouse', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_the_Lighthouse', 'To the Lighthouse', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The novel centres on the Ramsay family and their visits to the Isle of Skye in Scotland between 1910 and 1920.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'st-kilda', 'book', 'Where the World Ends', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Where_the_World_Ends', 'Where the World Ends', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Set in 1727 on the remote St Kilda archipelago in northern Scotland, the book follows a group of nine boys and three men who are abandoned on a sea stack while harvesting birds for an annual tradition.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'isle-of-skye', 'book', 'Wildfire at Midnight', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildfire_at_Midnight', 'Wildfire at Midnight', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Fashion model Gianetta Brooke goes on holiday to the Scottish island of Skye, only to find that her ex-husband, writer Nicholas Drury, is staying at the same hotel in Camasunary.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'wd-Q27508141', 'book', 'The Woman of Knockaloe', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Woman_of_Knockaloe', 'The Woman of Knockaloe', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Set on the Isle of Man during the First World War, a young woman finds herself drawn to one of the nearby German internees.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-3217444', 'book', 'The Wreck of the Zanzibar', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wreck_of_the_Zanzibar', 'The Wreck of the Zanzibar', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'She tells of her life on Bryher, one of Britain''s Scilly Isles, where her family''s survival depends on the mercy of the elements and the sea.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'isle-of-wight', 'book', 'The Trespasser (Lawrence novel)', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Trespasser_%28Lawrence_novel%29', 'The Trespasser (Lawrence novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Set mostly on the Isle of Wight, it tells the story of Siegmund, a married man with children, and his adulterous affair with Helena.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'isle-of-wight', 'book', 'The Night of the Triffids', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Night_of_the_Triffids', 'The Night of the Triffids', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The story begins on the Isle of Wight, 25 years after the events from The Day of the Triffids.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-2273838', 'book', 'Wide Open', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wide_Open_%28novel%29', 'Wide Open (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Set mostly on the Isle of Sheppey on the north coast of Kent on the Thames Estuary.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'scilly-st-marys', 'book', 'The Sleeping Sword', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sleeping_Sword', 'The Sleeping Sword', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The sword found on the island of Bryher, inspired Morpurgo''s Arthurian tale, set in the Scilly Isles, and is a story within a story.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-61921366', 'book', 'The Lighthouse Keeper''s Daughter', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lighthouse_Keeper%27s_Daughter_%28novel%29', 'The Lighthouse Keeper''s Daughter (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'It is set in two main locations: Longstone Lighthouse on the Northumberland Coast in England in the late 1830s and early 1840s, for which Gaynor uses historical fiction to describe the experiences of Grace Darling; and Newport, Rhode Island, particularly the Rose Island Light, in which the main protagonist is a fictional character in the late 1930s, Matilda Emmerson.', null, 'high', 'accepted');
insert into public.interest_memberships (category_slug, island_id, facet, title, source_url, source_title, licence, evidence, external_id, confidence, status) values
('island-books', 'rathlin', 'book', 'Turbulent Priests', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turbulent_Priests', 'Turbulent Priests', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Bateman''s usage of Rathlin Island (which he renamed "Wrathlin Island" in the novel) as the book''s setting led to Bateman being invited to unveil a "Writer''s Chair", commemorating writers of all origin and genre.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'guernsey', 'book', 'Just War', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Just_War_%28novel%29', 'Just War (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The story is set in Nazi Germany-occupied Guernsey, an example of invasion literature.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'jersey', 'book', 'Night of the Fox', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_of_the_Fox_%28novel%29', 'Night of the Fox (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'He is washed ashore on Jersey, and rescued by Hélène de Ville, wife of the Seigneur of Jersey, and Sean Gallagher, a former General in the Irish Army, who has retired in Jersey.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'mainland-shetland', 'book', 'A Stranger Came Ashore', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Stranger_Came_Ashore', 'A Stranger Came Ashore', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Set in the Shetland Islands in the north of Scotland, the plot revolves around a boy called Robbie Henderson, his family and a mysterious stranger named Finn Learson.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-4009637', 'book', 'Bridal Path', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridal_Path_%28novel%29', 'Bridal Path (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The story begins on Eorsa, an island in the Inner Hebrides of Scotland.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'mainland-shetland', 'book', 'Raven Black', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raven_Black', 'Raven Black', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Raven Black is the first in the "Shetland" mysteries, a series of eight novels by Cleeves, composed of two quartets, all set in Shetland.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-3601567', 'book', 'Venus as a Boy', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus_as_a_Boy_%28novella%29', 'Venus as a Boy (novella)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'It is set briefly in South Ronaldsay, Orkney, an island off the coast of Scotland though it is largely set in Soho, London.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'mainland-orkney', 'book', 'Vinland', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinland_%28novel%29', 'Vinland (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Vinland, published in 1992 by George Mackay Brown, is a historical novel set in the Orkney Islands in the early 11th century.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-6045552', 'book', 'Over the Bar', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Over_the_Bar', 'Over the Bar', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Over the Bar: A Personal Relationship with the GAA is a memoir by the Irish writer Breandán Ó hEithir, describing his early life on Inishmore, his education at University College, Galway (where he subsequently dropped out) and his long-time involvement with the Gaelic Athletic Association.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'lewis-and-harris', 'book', 'The Blackhouse', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Blackhouse', 'The Blackhouse', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', '== Plot == The action takes place mostly on the remote and weather-beaten Isle of Lewis off the coast of northern Scotland.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'lewis-and-harris', 'book', 'Great Northern?', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Northern%3F', 'Great Northern?', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Ransome also made a visit to the Isle of Lewis in the Outer Hebrides for a fishing trip and to research the area as the setting for the book.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-6045552', 'book', 'An Aran Keening', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_McNeillie', 'Andrew McNeillie', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'His prose memoir An Aran Keening tells of his stay on Inis Mór, just short of a year through 1968 and 1969.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'guernsey', 'book', 'Toilers of the Sea', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toilers_of_the_Sea', 'Toilers of the Sea', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', '== Plot summary == A woman arrives in Guernsey, with her son Gilliat, and buys a house...', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'isle-of-wight', 'book', 'England, England', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/England%2C_England', 'England, England', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Martha is now in her forties and is employed by the entrepreneur Sir Jack Pitman for a megalomaniacal project: Sir Jack aims to turn the Isle of Wight into a gigantic theme park which contains everything that people, especially tourists, consider to be quintessentially English, selected according to what Sir Jack himself approves of.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-castles', 'osm-relation-3834460', 'castle', 'Pennsylvania Castle', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennsylvania_Castle', 'Pennsylvania Castle', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia places it on this island. Pennsylvania Castle.', 'Q7163680', 'high', 'accepted'),
