('island-books', 'mainland-shetland', 'book', 'The Pirate', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pirate_(novel)', 'The Pirate (novel)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The setting is the southern tip of the main island of Shetland (which Scott visited in 1814), towards the end of the 17th century, with 1689 as the likely date of the main incidents.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-3217444', 'book', 'Why the Whales Came', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Why_the_Whales_Came', 'Why the Whales Came', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'It is set on the island of Bryher, one of the Isles of Scilly, off the coast of Cornwall, in the year 1914. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-6046655', 'book', 'Tide-race', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brenda_Chamberlain_(artist)', 'Brenda Chamberlain (artist)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'She won the first two Gold Medals awarded by the National Eisteddfod of Wales in the Fine Art category, for her paintings Girl with a Siamese Cat (1951) and The Cristin Children (1953), and her written works include Tide-race, a memoir of 15 years spent living on Bardsey Island. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-6046655', 'book', 'The Bones Beneath', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bardsey_Island', 'Bardsey Island', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Crime writer Mark Billingham set his 2014 novel, The Bones Beneath, on Bardsey. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-6046655', 'book', 'Twenty Thousand Saints', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bardsey_Island', 'Bardsey Island', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Her play Hugo was inspired by her stay, and she has produced two novels, Atyniad (English: Attraction), which won the prose medal at the 2006 Eisteddfod; and Twenty Thousand Saints, winner of the Oxfam Hay Prize, which tells how the women of the island, starved of men, turn to each other. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956937', 'book', 'Carette of Sark', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sark', 'Sark', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'John Oxenham wrote Carette of Sark (1907) and The Perilous Lovers (1924), historical novels largely set on Sark. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956937', 'book', 'The Perilous Lovers', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sark', 'Sark', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'John Oxenham wrote Carette of Sark (1907) and The Perilous Lovers (1924), historical novels largely set on Sark. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956937', 'book', 'A Maid of the Silver Sea', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sark', 'Sark', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'His 1910 novel A Maid of the Silver Sea uses the mines of Little Sark as its setting. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956937', 'book', 'Dame of Sark', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sark', 'Sark', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Dame of Sark, the memoirs of the 21st Seigneur Sibyl Mary Hathaway, who was present during the German occupation, were made into a play and television drama of the same name. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956937', 'book', 'The Last Kings of Sark', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sark', 'Sark', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The Last Kings of Sark: A Novel by Rosa Rankin-Gee is a 2015 coming-of-age story set in Sark. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956937', 'book', 'Iron Chamber of Memory', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sark', 'Sark', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The 2016 novel Iron Chamber of Memory by John C. Wright is set in Sark. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956897', 'book', 'Where Seagulls Dare', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herm', 'Herm', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Paul Sherman has written two collections of short stories set on the island: Where Seagulls Dare and One Flew Over the Puffin''s Nest. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-2956897', 'book', 'One Flew Over the Puffin''s Nest', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herm', 'Herm', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Paul Sherman has written two collections of short stories set on the island: Where Seagulls Dare and One Flew Over the Puffin''s Nest. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-12913146', 'book', 'A Line to Kill', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alderney', 'Alderney', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'In the 2021 novel A Line to Kill by Anthony Horowitz, the island is featured as the setting. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-3214114', 'book', 'Hell Bay', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tresco,_Isles_of_Scilly', 'Tresco, Isles of Scilly', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Hell Bay (1984), by Sam Llewellyn, is set on Tresco and fictionalises the events leading up to Augustus Smith taking ownership of the island. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-6188599', 'book', 'The Ghost of Grania O''Malley', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clare_Island', 'Clare Island', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Clare Island is the setting for the Michael Morpurgo book The Ghost of Grania O''Malley. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-376497843', 'book', 'Stargazing: Memoirs of a Young Lighthouse Keeper', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stargazing:_Memoirs_of_a_Young_Lighthouse_Keeper', 'Stargazing: Memoirs of a Young Lighthouse Keeper', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The book is a memoir about Hill''s time in the early 1970s as a young lighthouse keeper on the remote Scottish coast at the Pladda Lighthouse, Ailsa Craig Lighthouse, and the Hyskeir Lighthouse. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-relation-1571442', 'book', 'Stargazing: Memoirs of a Young Lighthouse Keeper', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stargazing:_Memoirs_of_a_Young_Lighthouse_Keeper', 'Stargazing: Memoirs of a Young Lighthouse Keeper', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The book is a memoir about Hill''s time in the early 1970s as a young lighthouse keeper on the remote Scottish coast at the Pladda Lighthouse, Ailsa Craig Lighthouse, and the Hyskeir Lighthouse. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'isle-of-skye', 'book', 'The Hill of the Red Fox', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allan_Campbell_McLean', 'Allan Campbell McLean', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'McLean was the writer of a number of children''s novels: The Hill of the Red Fox (1955; a contemporary spy story set in Skye); The Man of the House (1956; known as Storm over Skye in the US); Ribbon of Fire (1962; also set in Skye around the time of the Highland Clearances); Master of Morgana (1965); The Year of the Stranger (1971); and A Sound of Trumpets (1971). The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'isle-of-skye', 'book', 'Ribbon of Fire', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allan_Campbell_McLean', 'Allan Campbell McLean', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'McLean was the writer of a number of children''s novels: The Hill of the Red Fox (1955; a contemporary spy story set in Skye); The Man of the House (1956; known as Storm over Skye in the US); Ribbon of Fire (1962; also set in Skye around the time of the Highland Clearances); Master of Morgana (1965); The Year of the Stranger (1971); and A Sound of Trumpets (1971). The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-495525351', 'book', 'Stargazing: Memoirs of a Young Lighthouse Keeper', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stargazing:_Memoirs_of_a_Young_Lighthouse_Keeper', 'Stargazing: Memoirs of a Young Lighthouse Keeper', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The same sentence that places the memoir at Pladda and Hyskeir says it is about Hill''s time as a keeper at Ailsa Craig Lighthouse. An earlier pass rejected Ailsa Craig for lack of that sentence. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-4569530', 'book', 'The Outrun', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Outrun', 'The Outrun', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Later, she spends a winter on the Orkney island of Papa Westray in the RSPB''s house, which is normally only used in summer. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('island-books', 'osm-way-30782387', 'book', 'Arcam', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steep_Holm', 'Steep Holm', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The Steep Holm article says the island is the focal point of the 2018 crime thriller Arcam, by Jason Minick. The references list it as Arcam, J.Minick Books, 2018. The picture is a photograph of the island.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
