('unusual-wildlife', 'guernsey', 'wildlife', 'Loose Flowered orchid', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anacamptis_laxiflora', 'Anacamptis laxiflora', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The article says that in the United Kingdom the orchid is represented only on the Channel Islands, and that in Guernsey it is called Loose Flowered orchid.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('unusual-wildlife', 'isle-of-man', 'wildlife', 'Isle of Man cabbage', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coincya_monensis_subsp._monensis', 'Coincya monensis subsp. monensis', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The article says the plant grows around the coasts of the Isle of Man and was named because it was once abundant there. A second atlas record, wd-Q27508141, is the same island; the curated id is the one already used for wildlife there.', null, 'high', 'accepted'),
('unusual-wildlife', 'osm-relation-6045346', 'wildlife', 'South Stack fleawort', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tephroseris_integrifolia_subsp._maritima', 'Tephroseris integrifolia subsp. maritima', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'The article says the fleawort is endemic to Holyhead Island. The Holy Island (Anglesey) article says that island''s alternative English name is Holyhead Island, which matches this atlas record and not the other Holy Islands.', null, 'high', 'accepted');